Floor and roof outlines on Revit 2025 (sketch curve lists, span-direction
lines, arc box tolerance).

On Revit 2025 every floor came out as its record's bounding box, so floor
contours and sketch holes were lost (two user models and Autodesk's
rst_advanced 2025 sample among them). Three causes, each checked on those
files:

- scan_sketch_curve_lists read the Sketch's own curve list only on 2024.
  The 2025 layout is the same (owner at +77 past the element-data header,
  which partition_names already knows for 2025), so 2025 is listed too.
- A floor's span-direction arrow is one of its sketch lines and 2025 lists
  it with the boundary (a line straight across the floor, both ends free),
  so the loop solve rejected the whole floor. Curves with an end no other
  curve meets are dropped (repeatedly) before solving.
- An outline with arcs must span the record box within 0.001 ft, but
  Revit's record box comes from a coarse tessellation of the arc and stops
  short of it (0.0046 ft on a 6.2 ft radius). Arc outlines get 0.01 ft.

Drop this patch once upstream reads 2025 sketches itself.

